#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Prints the GitHub release notes: the version's CHANGELOG.md section, then the download guide.
#
# Usage: render-release-notes <X.Y.Z>      (run from the repository root)
# Output: Markdown on stdout.
# Exit codes: 0 done; 1 the changelog has no section for the version, or it is empty.
set -euo pipefail

SKILL=".claude/skills/release-new-version/SKILL.md"
version="${1:-}"

section="$(awk -v heading="## $version - " '
  /^## / { in_section = (index($0, heading) == 1); next }
  in_section { print }
' CHANGELOG.md | sed '/./,$!d')"

if ! grep -q '[^[:space:]]' <<<"$section"; then
  echo "render-release-notes: CHANGELOG.md has no entries for '$version' (see $SKILL)" >&2
  exit 1
fi

printf '%s\n' "$section"
cat <<NOTES

## Download the desktop app

| System | File |
| --- | --- |
| macOS, Apple silicon | \`mcp-guardrail-desktop-$version-macos-arm64.dmg\` |
| macOS, Intel | \`mcp-guardrail-desktop-$version-macos-x86_64.dmg\` |
| Linux x86_64 | \`mcp-guardrail-desktop-$version-linux-x86_64\` as \`.deb\`, \`.rpm\`, or \`.AppImage\` |
| Linux arm64 | \`mcp-guardrail-desktop-$version-linux-arm64\` as \`.deb\`, \`.rpm\`, or \`.AppImage\` |

The macOS app has an ad hoc signature, not a Developer ID, so macOS blocks it the first time. Drag it to Applications, then run:

\`\`\`sh
xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine "/Applications/MCP Guardrail.app"
\`\`\`

The app only reads the audit log.

## Download the proxy

| System | File |
| --- | --- |
| macOS, Apple silicon | \`mcp-guardrail-proxy-$version-macos-arm64.tar.gz\` |
| macOS, Intel | \`mcp-guardrail-proxy-$version-macos-x86_64.tar.gz\` |
| Linux x86_64 | \`mcp-guardrail-proxy-$version-linux-x86_64.tar.gz\` |
| Linux arm64 | \`mcp-guardrail-proxy-$version-linux-arm64.tar.gz\` |

Each archive holds one binary, \`mcp-guardrail-proxy\`. To wire it into your MCP client, follow [INSTALL.md](https://github.com/bostonaholic/mcp-guardrail-proxy/blob/v$version/INSTALL.md).
NOTES
